From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Name AVP 457 as ETSI TS 183 017 does

ETSI TS 183 017 V3.2.1 clause 7.3.8 defines AVP 457 (vendor ETSI) as
Latching-Indication, with the values LATCH (0) and RELATCH (1) the entry
already carries, and the AA-Request ABNF (clause 7.1.1) names it so;
table 7.3.1 prints Latching-indication. Requested-Information is ES 283
035's AVP 353.

Renaming an AVP renames its display filter field
(diameter.Requested-Information-457 becomes
diameter.Latching-Indication), so saved filters and profiles using the
old name need updating.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
index a48da2b..a72c4bb 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/etsie2e4.xml
@@ -209,7 +209,7 @@
 	<avp name="Reservation-Class" code="456" mandatory="may" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="no">
 		<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
 	</avp>
-	<avp name="Requested-Information-457" code="457" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
+	<avp name="Latching-Indication" code="457" mandatory="mustnot" vendor-bit="must" vendor-id="ETSI" may-encrypt="yes">
 		<type type-name="Enumerated"/>
 		<enum name="LATCH" code="0"/>
 		<enum name="RELATCH" code="1"/>
